# Implementation plan — Spec 1.17.0

## Summary

Remember the guest’s **requested page** before login. After Identity iframe success (Google or email/password), restore that page instead of always navigating to WebOnOne `/`. Preserve website `return_url` **path + query** (stop stripping to origin root in `parseWebsiteReturnUrl`). Invalid targets → default homepage. No open redirects; no secrets in return URLs.

Primary work: **WebOnOne FE** auth host. Secondary: **Website** CTA capture. Optional: **platform-nav** shared validation alignment. Identity login methods unchanged ([1.14.0](../1.14.0/README.md) embed + postMessage).

See [01-overview.md](./01-overview.md), [02-post-login-return-page.md](./02-post-login-return-page.md), [07-implementation-plan.md](./07-implementation-plan.md).

| Project | Touch |
|---------|--------|
| `webonone-v2/` | Fix return parse; wire `LoginPage` / postMessage restore / `WebsiteReturnRedirect` |
| `website/` | Auth-required CTAs pass current page into `getWebOnOneLoginUrl` |
| `packages/platform-nav/` | Optional align with `parseReturnUrl` (already keeps full URL) |
| `identity/` | No login-method changes |

